bibliograph-web (0.2.11-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.11 release: publish the XRPC surface the deployment serves.

    - Add GET community.lexicon.service.describe, answered at the edge with no
      database, auth or FEED_GENERATOR_DID: it returns
      { roles: ["appview","feedgen"], methods: [{ $type, value }] } naming all
      46 NSIDs this deployment answers. It is held to the dispatch registries
      and to happyview/scripts/xrpc/ by test/xrpc-surface.test.ts, so the list
      cannot describe a method that is not served.
    - Move the two books-wg NSIDs into the shared catalog/entity-methods
      registry and name the two PDS reads in pds-methods, so the dispatch and
      the description read one list instead of duplicating literals.
    - Attribute the new method in normalizeXrpcMethod instead of `other`.
    - No lexicon, HappyView script or deploy entry changed; the surface is the
      same 22 queries, 19 procedures and 10 record types.

