bibliograph-web (0.2.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.8 release: resolve an edition's format from Goodreads in the editor.

    - Add admin-only POST /admin/api/editions/<id>/resolve-format. It accepts
      ISBNs from the current unsaved form or falls back to the edition's
      persisted identifiers, filters them to checksum-valid ISBN-10/13 values,
      dedupes and caps the list at 10, and proxies the worker's /resolve-format
      response (including its 400/404/502) unchanged. No usable ISBN is a 400
      NoIsbns and a missing edition a 404.
    - Add a free-text Format field to the edition editor plus a Resolve from
      Goodreads button. The lookup fills the field and reports the ISBN used,
      with an explicit notice that the value is not saved until the operator
      saves the edition; there is no autosave, and lookup errors render inline.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:35:00 +0000

bibliograph-web (0.2.7-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.7 release: entity editors and catalog reports in the admin UI.

    - Add contributor and publisher editors at /admin/contributor/<id>/edit
      and /admin/publisher/<id>/edit (numeric id or percent-encoded at-URI),
      with admin-only GET/POST APIs under /admin/api/{contributors,publishers}
      /<id>. Updates are single-row transactions that preserve id, at_uri and
      createdAt, validate names, identifier pairs, descriptions, http(s) image
      URLs and strict YYYY-MM-DD dates, and use a content-revision token for
      409 conflicts. Catalog triggers queue the entity record and dependent
      editions; the routes never write pds_outbox.
    - Add Edit contributors and Edit publishers tabs with independent local
      search and links into the full editors.
    - Add the admin-only read-only Reports API: a registry endpoint plus one
      paginated result endpoint per report, with validated filters, stable
      ordering, full totals and JSON-safe rows. Reports cover missing covers,
      descriptions, languages, pages and published dates; identifier counts;
      contributors and publishers without identifiers; editions without
      contributors, publishers or CIDs; duplicate identifier pairs; and
      pending/stale publish outbox rows. Edition rows carry the canonical
      at-URI.
    - Add the Reports tab with report selection, identifier filters, table,
      totals and paging.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:45:00 +0000

bibliograph-web (0.2.6-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.6 release: admin edition editor, tabbed curation, input validation
    and universal XRPC CORS.

    - Add the edition editor: /admin/edition/<rkey>/edit and
      POST /admin/api/editions/<rkey> apply scalars, identifiers, contributor
      credits and publisher links to one edition in a single transaction.
      New entities reuse the ingest identity and mint their at-URI, and the
      catalog triggers queue the edition and entity records for publication.
    - Tab the admin page into provider search, publisher import, edition
      editing and merge, and add a local edition search for the editor that
      accepts a title, identifier, rkey or at-URI.
    - Validate editor input: language is optional and must be a well-formed
      BCP 47 tag canonicalized through Intl, and contributor roles must be
      known ONIX Codelist 17 codes; bad input is rejected per field.
    - Serve CORS on the whole XRPC surface: every valid NSID answers OPTIONS
      with 204 (GET/POST/OPTIONS; content-type, authorization, dpop, accept)
      and every response, including forwarded/proxied and error branches,
      carries Access-Control-Allow-Origin *, Vary: Origin and exposes
      dpop-nonce. Dispatch moves to an env-free module.

